The hudLayout folder is home to the theme-swapping engine: one HudThemeId preference (`'default' | 'slate-amber'`) persisted in localStorage via hudThemeStore.ts, and themeRegistry.ts's THEME_REGISTRY + resolveActiveTheme(id, viewportWidth) as the single source of truth for which lazy-loaded shell component (and whose styles) should render — layout shape and visual skin are one selectable unit per theme now, not the two independent settings this folder started as. hudWidgetRegistry.ts tracks which plugin currently owns each named compact-HUD slot (`hud.bottomStrip`, `hud.rightColumn`), broadcasting `shatteredarchive:hud-widget-updated` on every publish/clear — a shared extension point any theme's shell can use, not slate-amber-specific. This folder integrates with the broader application via MainContainer (calls resolveActiveTheme every render to pick ActiveShell + apply that resolved theme's styles, and — separately, via each theme's optional `onActivate` — auto-enable whichever core plugin that theme depends on; `slate-amber` auto-enables `world-time-and-identity`) and the settings UI (GraphicsSettingsModal's single Theme selector), plus pluginHost.ts and CompactWidgetSlot for the slot registry.
